        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0971f38d-7972-57ea-b9b7-eca1b65ae094",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johann Nicolaus von Dreyse\n- Products: Dreyse needle gun, Lebel Model 1886 rifle, Mauser M 98, M16, Fusil Mle 1886 M93\n- Concepts: Rotating bolt\n\nFacts:\n- Johann Nicolaus von Dreyse developed the Dreyse needle gun, the first rotating bolt firearm, in 1836.\n- The Dreyse needle gun locked using the bolt handle rather than lugs on the bolt head.\n- The Lebel Model 1886 rifle was the first rotating bolt rifle with two lugs on the bolt head.\n- The Mauser M 98 and the M16 used lugs on the bolt head, unlike the Dreyse needle gun.\n- In 1893, the Lebel Model 1886 rifle received a bolt modification, after which it was also known as the Fusil Mle 1886 M93.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "20732504-2ee2-5ebe-a028-af4c8d284942",
        "text": "Page: Rotating bolt. Sentence: Johann Nicolaus von Dreyse developed the first rotating bolt firearm, the \"Dreyse needle gun\" in 1836.\nPage: Rotating bolt. Sentence: The Dreyse locked using the bolt handle rather than lugs on the bolt head like the Mauser M 98 or M16.\nPage: Rotating bolt. Sentence: The first rotating bolt rifle with two lugs on the bolt head was the Lebel Model 1886 rifle.\nPage: Lebel Model 1886 rifle. Sentence: The Lebel Model 1886 rifle (French: Fusil Modèle 1886 dit \"Fusil Lebel\") is also known as the \"Fusil Mle 1886 M93\", after a bolt modification was added in 1893.",
